│     The bug in `fastapi` regarding the separation of schemas with nested     │
│ models was identified as being related to how `get_schema_from_model_field`  │
│ handles nested models when `separate_input_output_schemas` is set to `True`. │
│ The function `get_schema_from_model_field` is located in                     │
│ `fastapi/_compat/main.py` and is used in `fastapi/openapi/utils.py` to       │
│ generate schemas for various parts of the OpenAPI specification. The issue   │
│ is that it doesn't correctly handle nested models by generating separate     │
│ schemas for them, leading to incorrect schema definitions in the OpenAPI     │
│ output. To fix this, `get_schema_from_model_field` should be updated to      │
│ check if a field is a nested model and, if so, generate a separate schema    │
│ for it and reference it in the parent schema, while respecting the           │
│ `separate_input_output_schemas` flag.                                        │
